<ChartsRuntimeNotice />
<DocsExample TExample="PieBasicExample" Title="Pie with legend" Description="A pie shows how a whole divides into parts. Add NTLegend so readers can match each slice to its category and toggle slices on and off." />
<DocsExample TExample="PieManyLabelsExample" Title="Many slices and long labels" Description="58 slices, five with 150-character labels. Pick a legend position to see how the pie keeps its size: long labels wrap so no legend item is wider than 30% of the chart, top and bottom legends scroll sideways after MaxRows rows, and left, right and floating legends stay within 30% of the chart width and scroll up and down." />
<DocsExample TExample="PieDonutExample" Title="Donut" Description="InnerRadiusRatio cuts a hole in the middle, which keeps the focus on slice sizes rather than on the area they cover." />
<DocsExample TExample="PieDataLabelsExample" Title="Data labels and formatting" Description="DataLabelFormat controls how each slice value is printed. Use it to add units, and turn off hover explosion when labels must stay put." />
<DocsExample TExample="PieTooltipExample" Title="Custom tooltip" Description="TooltipInfoSelector replaces the default tooltip with your own header and lines, so you can show context the raw value does not carry." />
<DocsExample TExample="PieSliceClickExample" Title="Slice clicks" Description="OnClick reports the data item behind the slice the user selected. Use it to drive details elsewhere on the page." />
